A||||8||Alex4mula||Should I buy this Formula??||||1||
Z||000000||Alex4mula||08-03-2000||04:39 PM||||I need someone else opinion. I went to see this 88 Formula. It is auto with power nothing except cruise control. The interior cloth is in excellent condition. Seats are perfect. Some A/C vents fins are broken, the shifter boot and one ash tray door is broken and the alternator/oil gage pod is split. The front trunk is very clean. Rear trunk is almost new. Now about exterior, the car looks like it was painted to sell. It has a nice shiny black paint with all the decals. The rear bumper has a damage with a poor repair but from far looks in shape. Paint is dull in that area. The right rearview mirror is a little bent to the inside. The rear spoiler is sagging and one of the post looks repaired with cracks. Overall from 15 feet looks good. Suspension is shot (needs shocks) and for some reason all end links rubber are broken down to nothing. You can move the front sway bar. Tires are ok but different brands. Needs a brake job and maybe rotors. A/C works but does not cool too much. The worst part is the engine. It has a serious misfire and seems to run on 4 of the 6 cylinders. It does not smokes. Could be wires/sparks, etc. but to me I think it is bad. The guy is asking $1500. I would offer $900 saving the other $600 for brakes repair and a quickie repair in the V6. I have a set of reconditioned heads. My plan is for a later V8. What do you think? Is the price fair for a Formula? Will try to post picture. Thanks and sorry for the long post.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||08-03-2000||05:11 PM||||Here is the picture... 6th try!.. I think it does not work for me... :-(<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/fieroforum.pip" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/fieroforum.pip</A> <p>[This message has been edited by Alex4mula (edited 08-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||08-03-2000||05:17 PM||||Offer him $800 for it and if he does not take the offer leave it because it sounds to me like that car has been through hell. Don't take the car if you are not mechanically inclined or are not willing to work on it because to have someone work on it for you is going to be expensive. If the car has been in a major accident than stay clear of it also. Just my opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||08-03-2000||05:24 PM||||I checked the car very well and it is all straight. No major accident. I did my own 3.4 trasplant so replacing the short block with a cheap 3.1 is no problem. I'm just not sure about the price for its condition. I saw another selling for $2000 that I would not pay $200. This one looks clean. How much depreciate not having a good running engine? <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/fieroforum.pip" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/fieroforum.pip</A> ||||reg||1
