Z||000006||Raydar||08-03-2000||07:45 PM||||Alex,<BR>I dunno man. Sounds like it's had the crap beat out of it. Been neglected. <BR>Imagine all the stuff you haven't found out about, yet.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  Pull back the sides of the trunk liner and check for rust. <BR>I'd offer him $600. If he says no, give him your number and ask him to call if he doesn't sell it. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 08-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fformula88||08-03-2000||11:04 PM||||Sounds to me like its about ready to be stripped down for parts.  If he lets it go cheap, go for it.  Even if its a slow process getting it up and working, it can be done.  But from what you described, it sounds like it was beaten.  Anything over $800 and you should be able to find something in better shape.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Alex4mula||08-04-2000||09:19 AM||||Well guys, thank you very much for your comments. I'll call the guy and offer $800 and to call me if he does not sell. I know that anyone without mechanic skills won't buy it. Or only a real Fiero lover...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
